UserController (Controllers/UserController.cs):
This controller manages user-related operations such as registration and login. It interacts
with the UserService to perform these operations.

Functions:
1. public async Task<IActionResult> Register([FromBody] User user)
. Registers a new user.
. Checks if the user already exists by email using the GetUserByEmailAsync method from
the UserService.
. If the user already exists, returns a 409 Conflict response with the message "User already

exists."
. If the user does not exist, registers the user using the RegisterUserAsync method from the
UserService.
. Returns a 200 OK response with a success message and the user ID of the registered user.

2. public async Task<IActionResult> Login([FromBody] LoginModel model)
. Authenticates a user login.
. Validates the login request by checking if the model is null.
. Retrieves the user by email using the GetUserByEmailAsync method from the UserService.
. Compares the retrieved user's password with the password provided in the model.
. If the user or password is invalid, returns a 401 Unauthorized response with the message
"Invalid email or password."
. If the user and password are valid, generates a JWT token for the user using the
GenerateJwtTokenAsync method from the UserService.
. Returns a 200 OK response with the generated JWT token in the response body.
. Returns a 500 Internal Server Error response if there is an issue generating the JWT token.
Note: All endpoints should be authorized by JWT token except login and register.

