AuthService (Services/auth.service.ts):
This service handles user authentication, registration, and authorization for the application.
It communicates with the backend API and manages authentication state within the client
application.

Functions:
1. register(user: User): Observable<any>
Registers a new user.
o Sends a POST request with user data to the backend API endpoint
/api/register.
o Stores user data in local storage if registration is successful.
o Catches and handles any errors that occur during the registration process.
2. login(email: string, password: string): Observable<any>
o Logs in a user.
o Sends a POST request with login credentials to the backend API endpoint
/api/login.
Decodes the received token and stores the token, user ID, user role, and user
name in local storage.
Catches and handles any errors that occur during the login process.

BookingService (Services/booking.service.ts)
This service handles booking-related operations such as adding, retrieving, updating, and
deleting bookings. It communicates with the backend API and includes authorization
headers for secure access.
Functions:
1. addBooking(booking: Booking)
Adds a new booking.
Retrieves the authentication token from local storage.
o Sets the appropriate headers, including the authorization token.
Sends a POST request with the booking data to the backend API endpoint
/api/booking.

2. getBookingsByUserld()
o Retrieves bookings for the current user.
Retrieves the authentication token and user ID from local storage.
Sets the appropriate headers, including the authorization token.
o Sends a GET request to the backend API endpoint /api/user/{userld}.

3. updateBooking(booking: any)
Updates an existing booking.
o Retrieves the booking ID and authentication token from local storage.
Sets the appropriate headers, including the authorization token.
Sends a PUT request with the booking data to the backend API endpoint
/api/booking/{bookingld}.

4. deleteBooking(bookingld: number)
Deletes a booking by its ID.
o Retrieves the authentication token from local storage.
Sets the appropriate headers, including the authorization token.
Sends a DELETE request to the backend API endpoint
